UID:3e0bd2f6f168e5ff@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · Call 6:00 PM · 7:00 PM–7:45 PM · Robinson 
 Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 6:00 PM: dancers must b
 e checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 5:45 PM. BA: Call Time
  is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minute
 s before Call Time.\nACT I Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair an
 d Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHANG
 E — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal ar
 e the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1x
 WFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP f
 or Rats: Rats — Costume (you provide): Male: Black tights\, black fitt
 ed t-shirt Female: Black Seamless Tights\, Black or Flesh tone Camisole 
 Leotard\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair:
  Male: Hair out of the eyes Female: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA
  provides): Gloves\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Powde
 r matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shadow applied to the creas
 e with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black 
 mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply 
 plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• 
  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights a
 nd flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle co
 stume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabr
 ics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume dam
 age at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n•  Never
  throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their 
 elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costu
 me\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any cost
 ume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in costume and
  shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume durin
 g its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne 
 while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast me
 mber\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume
 \, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from thei
 r assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby 
 pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n•  Re
 turn all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with an
 y and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do no
 t pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or 
 stain costumes.
